d1` -> `False`\n`True and False` -> `False`. Correct.\n\nLet's check the original again: `start1 <= end2 and start2 <= end1`.\nThe issue is the `<=`.\nIf I change it to `<`:\n`return start1 < end2 and start2 < end1`\n\nLet's test this logic with the test cases.\n1. `bookings_conflict(\"2026-03-05\", \"2026-03-10\", \"2026-03-10\", \"2026-03-12\")`\n   `start1=\"2026-03-05\", end1=\"2026-03-10\", start2=\"2026-03-10\", end2=\"2026-03-12\"`\n   `start1 < end2` -> `\"2026-03-05\" < \"2026-03-12\"` -> `True`\n   `start2 < end1` -> `\"2026-03-10\" < \"2026-03-10\"` -> `False`\n   `True and False` -> `False`. (Matches expectation)\n\n2. `bookings_conflict(\"2026-03-10\", \"2026-03-12\", \"2026-03-05\", \"2026-03-10\")`\n   `start1=\"2026-03-10\", end1=\"2026-03-12\", start2=\"2026-03-05\", end2=\"2026-03-10\"`\n   `start1 < end2` -> `\"2026-03-10\" < \"2026-03-10\"` -> `False`\n   `start2 < end1` -> `\"2026-03-05\" < \"2026-03-12\"` -> `True`\n   `False and True` -> `False`. (Matches expectation)\n\n3. `bookings_conflict(\"2026-03-05\", \"2026-03-10\", \"2026-03-08\", \"2026-03-12\")`\n   `start1=\"2026-03-05\", end1=\"2026-03-10\", start2=\"2026-03-08\", end2=\"2026-03-12\"`\n   `start1 < end2` -> `\"2026-03-05\" < \"2026-03-12\"` -> `True`\n   `start2 < end1` -> `\"2026-03-08\" < \"2026-03-10\"` -> `True`\n   `True and True` -> `True`. (Matches expectation)\n\n4. `bookings_conflict(\"2026-03-05\", \"2026-03-10\", \"2026-03-05\", \"2026-03-10\")`\n   `start1=\"2026-03-05\", end1=\"2026-03-10\", start2=\"2026-03-05\", end2=\"2026-03-10\"`\n   `start1 < end2` -> `\"2026-03-05\" < \"2026-03-10\"` -> `True`\n   `start2 < end1` -> `\"2026-03-05\" < \"2026-03-10\"` -> `True`\n   `True and True` -> `True`. (Matches expectation)\n\n5. `bookings_conflict(\"2026-03-01\", \"2026-03-05\", \"2026-03-20\", \"2026-03-25\")`\n   `start1=\"2026-03-01\", end1=\"2026-03-05\", start2=\"2026-03-20\", end2=\"2026-03-25\"`\n   `start1 < end2` -> `\"2026-03-01\" < \"2026-03-25\"` -> `True`\n   